The Visual Meaning Layer reasons over creative knowledge.

Creators extend that reasoning through Custom Creative Intent.

Together they form the Creative Brief.

---

# Design Principles

## Semantic Reasoning

The VML reasons about creative meaning rather than renderer behavior.

Its purpose is to understand creative intent.

---

## Probabilistic Guidance

Creative recommendations are probabilistic.

They suggest possibilities rather than prescribe outcomes.

The creator remains the final decision maker.

---

## Human-Centered Reasoning

The Visual Meaning Layer recommends.

The creator decides.

Semantic reasoning augments human creativity rather than replacing it.

---

## Creative Freedom

Every recommendation is optional.

Creators may override, ignore, extend, or contradict any recommendation
through Custom Creative Intent.

Unexpected, surreal, contradictory, or experimental ideas remain
first-class citizens within VizClick.

---

## Renderer Independence

The Visual Meaning Layer never contains:

- prompt syntax
- renderer parameters
- optimization strategies
- model-specific keywords

These responsibilities belong exclusively to Renderer Adapters.

---

## Knowledge Driven

All reasoning originates from Creative Concepts and their semantic
relationships stored within the Creative Knowledge Ecology.

The VML reasons over knowledge.

It does not redefine knowledge.

---

## Explainability

Every recommendation should be traceable to the Creative Concepts and
Relationships that produced it.

Creative reasoning should remain transparent rather than opaque.

---

## Extensibility

The reasoning implementation may evolve over time.

Graph reasoning, probabilistic inference, neural reasoning, symbolic AI,
or future approaches may all implement the same architectural
responsibility.

The architecture remains stable.

---

# Consequences

## Positive

- Intelligent creative assistance
- Explainable recommendations
- Semantic consistency
- Renderer independence
- Unlimited creative freedom
- Transparent reasoning
- Flexible implementations
- Future-proof architecture

## Trade-offs

- Introduces an additional reasoning layer
- Requires semantic relationship maintenance
- Requires probabilistic evaluation

These trade-offs are accepted because they provide a more intelligent,
transparent, and collaborative creative experience.

---

# Philosophy

Creative knowledge is static.

Creative intent is dynamic.

The Visual Meaning Layer bridges the two.

It transforms reusable knowledge into meaningful creative guidance.

Creators extend that guidance through Custom Creative Intent.

VizClick assists creativity.

It never replaces imagination.

---

# Guiding Principle

> The Visual Meaning Layer understands creative intent.
>
> The creator defines creative direction.